The problem with my VAXstation 4000-60 is probably located in the LCG color
graphics board. After I pulled the LCG board the system booted without
reporting an error message. With the LCG installed it returned this error:

?? 010  2  LCG   0112

>>> B/1

?33 UNXINT
004   80000022   037E7A0C   E0046844   00000000
0814CB05   00001E83   E0046830   041F0000

Without service documentation there's no way to interpret all that other
than that the LCG board may be at fault. There is an interesting difference
with the VAXstation 4000-90A. If the graphics board in the 90A is removed,
faulty r improperly installed then VMS no longer recognizes the 90A as a
VAXstation (let alone a model 4000-90A) and VMS refuses to load a license.
The VAXstation 4000-60 apparently is less strict.

Even though I usually run DECwindows on a ReflectionX system it would be
nice to have a working graphics controller again. If you happen to have an
LCG board (or SPXg) that you no longer need, please let me know. Remove
.nieuw from the email address.
TIA,
Hans Vlems
The Netherlands




