> >>I'm a bit confused about BOOT, HALT and RESTART (or the equivalent

For VAX 3100:

BOOT : automatically load system software upon power up and after OS system failure.

RESTART: "To set the recovery actions to automatic restart should the system
go down"

The default is BOOT ( SET HALT 2)


Reading some of the old manuals I had, there was mention of some of the models
that had capability to restart after a power failure if the memory had been
preserved with battery backup. But the 3100 doesn't really have that
capability unless it is undocumented/hidden.

Seems to me that the guy who write the 3100 hardware manual was purposefully
very vague on the "RESTART" simply because nobody knew what it did :-) :-) :-)
:-) ;-)


