>   supported it on 11/780, but I've never actually seen one.
> 
>   And not all processing is interactive.  Yes, you would loose all
>   networked connections, but everything else would be OK.

The UNIBUS Ethernet controller was a DEUNA.  (I think this was later
replaced by a DELUA.)

We had a 780 and 785 clustered.  Almost all terminal access was via LAT
and terminal servers.

The 780 had one or two DZ-11s, but these were only used were permanent
connections were required.  For example, one of them was used for a 20ma
connection to a Data General machine.

The 785 had no direct serial interfaces at all.  (Except the console.)

