That sounds exactly like sticky shed. It is not really a shedding
problem, it is caused by the urithane binder hydrolysing over time and
forming a sticky polymer. 8 hrs in a 115-120F dry ovan as first step
should help lots.

Blue ring CDCs, DEC branded tape are 'orrid, gold ring CDC is way
better.

BTW, don't let the tape stop without slipping a bit of teflon film
over the head. It will stick solid! And then you rip a stripe of
oxide off to clean the head... :( Also, streaming drives are
bad news for this. They can lose control of the tape in most
spectacular ways, none of them good for your tape. A slow vacum
column drive is what is best for this.

