Prpbably the best method is by using a cluster wide LAT service. If you have
a cluster with nodes AAP and NOOT then the standard (default) LAT service
names are the same as the nodenames. It is perfectly alright to create a
third LAT service, say MIES, that exists on both cluster members. Define
MIES as the preferred service (possibly with the attribute autoconnnect
enabled) and all users wil be connected to the the service MIES. Since that
service is offered by two nodes, users are evenly distributed over AAP and
NOOT. If you want to connect them to one node only, modify the static rating
for the nodes. Low values make the node less likely to be selected.

